// Antifrost — thirty-five hills for the cold season.
//
// Legend: `#` rock, `,` dirt, `.` tunnel, `@` player start,
// uppercase `W R Y G B` beds (W is the player's), lowercase `r y g b` wild ants.
//
// Par policy: twenty-eight hills carry their BFS optimum — found by
// exhaustive search, so no shorter win exists (solver::tests::
// solve_all_shipped re-proves it every run). Seven hills — the five
// four-ant runs Deadfall, Winter Quarters, Deep Cellar, Ashfall,
// Ember Deep, plus Hearth Row and Ninefold — have spaces or
// lock-timings that outrun any cap we can carry, so their pars are
// routes that the `solver::tests::hand_route_wins_*` tests replay move
// by move: beatable, not claimed unbeatable. `solver::hunt_route` (a
// layered beam search) is what finds most of those routes; Ninefold
// was worked out by hand on paper and proven by the same replay.

